          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general General
          %p
            A
            %strong connective spectrum
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+object"} connective object
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"}
                stable
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group+of+a+spectrum"} homotopy groups
            in all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
            degrees are
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+groups"} trivial
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{\bullet \lt 0}(S) \,=\, 0
          %p These are equivalently:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+spaces"}> infinite loop spaces
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} grouplike
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+%E2%88%9E-groups"}> abelian ∞-groups
                \.
          %p
            Connective spectra form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mo ⊃
                  %mi ConnectSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Top \stackrel{\supset}{\leftarrow} ConnectSp(Top) \hookrightarrow Sp(Top)
                  \\,.
          %p
            There are objects in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            infinitely many times. These are the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong non-connective spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of negative degree. The connective ones are precisely those for which all negative degree
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            vanish.
          %h3#strict Strict
          %p
            There is a subclass of connective spectra that are equivalent to possibly-more-familiar objects, namely nonnegatively graded
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            that are not only connective spectra but even have a
            %em strict
            symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            structure with non-negatively graded
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Ch
                            %mo +
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi Dold
                              %mo −
                              %mi Kan
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi nerve
                        %mtd
                          %mi ConnectSp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mi Grp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mn ∞
                          %mi Grpd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ∂
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 1
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ∂
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 0
                          %mo →
                          %mn 0
                          %mo →
                          %mn 0
                          %mo →
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↦
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Ch_+ &amp;\stackrel{Dold-Kan \; nerve}{\to}&amp;
                  ConnectSp(\infty Grp) \subset \infty Grpd
                  \\\
                  (\cdots A_2 \stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_1 \stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_0 \to 0 \to 0 \to \cdots)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{}{\mapsto}&amp;
                  N(A_\bullet)
                  }
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            groups of the chain complex correspond precisely to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          %p
            The free stabilization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of non-negatively graded chain complexes is simpy the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            of arbitrary chain complexes. There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} stable Dold-Kan correspondence
            that identifies these with special objects in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(Top)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Ch
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi Dold
                              %mo −
                              %mi Kan
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi nerve
                        %mtd
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mi Grp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ∂
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 1
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ∂
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 0
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ∂
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ∂
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 2
                          %mo →
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↦
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Ch &amp;\stackrel{Dold-Kan \; nerve}{\to}&amp;
                  Sp(\infty Grp)
                  \\\
                  (\cdots A_2 \stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_1 \stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_0 \stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_{-1}
                  \\stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_{-2} \to \cdots)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{}{\mapsto}&amp;
                  N(A_\bullet)
                  }
          %p So it is the homologically nontrivial parts of the chain complexes in negative degree that corresponds to the non-connectiveness of a spectrum.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#InclusionIntoAllSpectra Inclusion into all spectra
          %p The inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Spectra
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Spectra_{\geq 0} \hookrightarrow Spectra
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(∞,1)-category
            of connective spectra into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-category of spectra
            preserves small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} (∞,1)-colimits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spectra_{\geq 0}
            is generated under small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} (∞,1)-colimits
            by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
          %p
            These statements prolong to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+spectra"} sheaves of spectra
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectral+Schemes"}> Lurie, "Spectral Schemes", example 1.23
            )
          %h3#ConnectiveCover Connective cover
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#InclusionIntoAllSpectra"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} coreflective sub-(∞,1)-category
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-category of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{\geq 0}
            from spectra to connective spectra is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+cover"} connective cover
            construction, part of the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/t-structure"} t-structure
            on spectra (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "t-structure#CanonicalTStructureOnSpectra"} there
